ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether Alignment=E2=80=99s third-quar=
ter reserve development confirms stabilization, and whether other MA carriers=
 identify retrospective hospital billing=E2=80=94not admissions alone=E2=80=
=94as a 2027 pricing and benefit-design factor.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-3" name=3D"story-3" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>3. ACCESS creates a Medicare paym=
ent path for technology-supported chronic care</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS expanded the ACCESS Model to inclu=
de heart failure, COPD, substance-use disorders and nicotine dependence begin=
ning in spring 2027. The model ties payments to specified health outcomes and=
 permits participating organizations to use virtual care, coaching, remote mo=
nitoring, connected devices and wearables. CMS said 160 organizations will pa=
rticipate at launch and that payers representing 165 million people have pled=
ged to adopt aligned outcomes-based structures; MA members are not eligible f=
or the Medicare model itself. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-=
releases/cms-adds-medicare-options-help-people-manage-substance-use-disorder-=
heart-failure-other-common" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;=
">CMS, =E2=80=9CCMS Adds Medicare Options to Help People Manage Substance Use=
 Disorder, Heart Failure, and Other Common Chronic Conditions,=E2=80=9D Septe=
mber 15, 2026</a>). (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/c=
ms-adds-medicare-options-help-people-manage-substance-use-disorder-heart-fail=
ure-other-common" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">cms.gov<=
/a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">ACCESS moves digital chronic care beyo=
nd employer and MA pilot budgets into a defined Original Medicare reimburseme=
nt pathway. The opportunity extends to monitoring devices, patient engagement=
, referrals, outcomes measurement and data exchange with primary-care workflo=
ws.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">However, this is not fee-for-technolog=
y reimbursement. Vendors must demonstrate CMS-defined outcomes and manage att=
ribution, clinical escalation and longitudinal data. Platforms capable of sup=
porting multiple conditions and payers should have an advantage over single-c=
ondition applications.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Track-level payment methodology, outco=
me thresholds, beneficiary attribution and evidence that commercial and MA pa=
yers convert their pledges into implemented contracts.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-4" name=3D"story-4" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>4. GENEROUS shifts Medicaid drug =
savings into rebate operations</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">All states, the District of Columbia a=
nd Puerto Rico applied to the GENEROUS Model; 40 states and Puerto Rico had s=
igned participation agreements by September 18. Participating manufacturers p=
rovide covered outpatient drugs at most-favored-nation pricing through supple=
mental rebates invoiced by states, with CMS reducing the federal Medicaid sha=
re to reflect its portion. CMS estimates $64.3 billion of taxpayer savings ov=
er ten years. Remaining states have until September 30, 2026, to sign. (<a hr=
ef=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/cms-announces-participants-=
landmark-medicaid-drug-payment-model-bring-down-drug-costs-most" style=3D"col=
or:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, =E2=80=9CCMS Announces Participan=
ts in Landmark Medicaid Drug Payment Model,=E2=80=9D September 18, 2026</a>).=
 (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/cms-announces-partic=
ipants-landmark-medicaid-drug-payment-model-bring-down-drug-costs-most" style=
=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">cms.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The immediate technology opportunity i=
s rebate invoicing, price validation and reconciliation=E2=80=94not necessari=
ly higher MCO margins. States can rebase pharmacy capitation or require pass-=
through treatment, meaning savings may accrue primarily to state and federal =
governments.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The model could reduce the strategic v=
alue of opaque PBM spread economics while increasing demand for auditable man=
ufacturer-rebate administration. Actual magnitude remains uncertain because p=
articipating manufacturers, covered products and state contract treatment wil=
l determine realized savings.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">State MCO contract amendments and disc=
losure of participating manufacturers and covered drugs.</p>
